<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Insubres</h1><p class="st-meta">600 BCE – 194 BCE (approx.) · capital Mediolanum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Celtic people of the Po plain who founded Milan and were the strongest Gaulish opponents of Rome in northern Italy.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a> says <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/celts">Celts</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bellovesus">Bellovesus</a> crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> around 600 BCE and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Mediolanum</a>, the later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Milan</a>, on land already called Insubrian. Archaeology shows the local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golasecca-culture">Golasecca culture</a>, which already spoke a Celtic language, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lepontic-language">Lepontic</a>, absorbing larger Gaulish migrations in the 5th and 4th centuries BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Insubres formed a tribal state with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Mediolanum</a> as a central place, ruled by warrior aristocrats and kings. They lived in villages and fortified centres, farmed the rich plain and minted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> coins imitating those of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/massalia">Massalia</a>. They often led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cisalpine-gaul">Cisalpine Gauls</a> in war, joining the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/boii">Boii</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 225 BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> defeated them at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-telamon">Telamon</a> in 225 BCE and at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-clastidium">Clastidium</a> in 222 BCE, and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Mediolanum</a>. They backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>, but after defeats in 196 and 194 BCE they accepted a treaty. Their land was gradually Romanised, gaining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> and then full citizenship in the 1st century BCE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 600 BCE – 194 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:47.76%;width:8.08%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 BCE – 194 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mediolanum</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Insubrians</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-397&amp;focus=insubres" aria-label="Insubres on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4898 574 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Insubres lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5218 830L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5218 830h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5218 830h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mediolanum. <a href="/atlas?year=-397&amp;focus=insubres">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

